king among young HIV-seronegative gay and bisexual men</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr Hum Retrovirol</source><year>1998</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9732071</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Strathdee</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Martindale</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cornelisse</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Craib</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schechter</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Shaughnessy</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogg</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV infection and risk behaviours among young gay and bisexual men in Vancouver</article-title><source>CMAJ</source><year>2000</year><volume>162</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11216194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abramson</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>WINPEPI (PEPI-for-Windows): computer programs for epidemiologists</article-title><source>Epidemiol Perspect Innov</source><year>2004</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>6</fpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.brixtonhealth.com/pepi4windows.html"/><comment>(Accessed March 13, 2007)</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15606913</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1742-5573-1-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koblin</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chesney</surname><given-names>MA</give